---
import DocLayout from "../../../layouts/DocLayout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
---

<DocLayout
  title="Local MCP quickstart"
  description="Copy-paste setup for running rob-mcp from a source checkout as a free local stdio MCP server with Bun and your own Robinhood Chain RPC."
>
  <p class="eyebrow">Getting started</p><h1>Run rob-mcp locally</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Local stdio MCP is free. It talks directly to your configured RPC and does not use the hosted
    x402 paywall.
  </p>
  <h2>1. Install from the source repository</h2>
  <CodeBlock
    code={`git clone https://github.com/oyusypenko/rob-mcp.git
cd rob-mcp
bun install --frozen-lockfile`}
    label="Source checkout"
  />
  <h2>2. Provide an RPC and start the server</h2>
  <CodeBlock
    code={`export RPC_URL_4663="https://your-robinhood-chain-rpc.example"
bun run dev`}
    label="Run stdio MCP"
  />
  <h2>3. Add it to your MCP client</h2>
  <CodeBlock
    code={`{
  "mcpServers": {
    "rob-mcp": {
      "command": "bun",
      "args": ["/absolute/path/to/rob-mcp/src/cli.ts"],
      "env": {
        "RPC_URL_4663": "https://your-robinhood-chain-rpc.example"
      }
    }
  }
}`}
    label="Client configuration"
  />
  <h2>4. Make the first call</h2>
  <p>
    Ask your client to call <code>list_stock_tokens</code> with <code
      >{"{"}"search":"AAPL"{"}"}</code
    >. It is implemented, free, and does not require a price-liveness source.
  </p>
  <div class="callout">
    The npm package is not published yet. Use the source-checkout commands above; the server
    verifies the RPC’s live chain ID at boot and fails closed on a mismatch.
  </div>
</DocLayout>
